valid, template mode
  (accepted)
valid, local only
  (accepted)
format missing
  ERROR unsupported auth config format: none (this build reads format 1)
kind unknown
  ERROR directory has kind 'kerberos'; this build implements 'ldap'
host missing
  ERROR directory has no 'host'
security missing
  ERROR directory has no 'security'; it must be 'ldaps', 'starttls' or 'plain', and there is no default because a cleartext bind must be a word somebody typed
security unknown
  ERROR directory has security 'none'; it must be 'ldaps', 'starttls' or 'plain'
port not a whole number
  ERROR directory has 'port' of '636.5'; it must be a whole number of at least 1
both ways to find a user
  ERROR directory sets both 'user_dn_template' and 'user_search'; it names exactly one way to find a user
neither way to find a user
  ERROR directory sets neither 'user_dn_template' nor 'user_search'; it names exactly one way to find a user
template without a placeholder
  ERROR 'user_dn_template' contains no '{user}', so every login would construct the same DN
user_search without a base
  ERROR 'user_search' has no 'base'
user_search without a filter
  ERROR 'user_search' has no 'filter'
user_search filter without a placeholder
  ERROR 'user_search' filter contains no '{user}', so it would match the same entry for every login
user_search scope unknown
  ERROR 'user_search' has scope 'deep'; it must be 'base', 'one' or 'sub'
bind_password without a bind_dn
  ERROR directory sets 'bind_password' with no 'bind_dn'
group_strategy missing
  ERROR directory has no 'group_strategy'; it must be 'memberof' (read the attribute) or 'search' (find groups whose 'member' is the user's DN), and there is no default because stock OpenLDAP populates no memberOf and zero groups is a legitimate answer
group_strategy unknown
  ERROR directory has group_strategy 'guess'; it must be 'memberof' or 'search'
search strategy without a group_base
  ERROR group_strategy 'search' needs a 'group_base' to search under
group_filter without a placeholder
  ERROR 'group_filter' contains no '{dn}', so it would return the same groups for every user
group_names unknown
  ERROR directory has group_names 'cn'; it must be 'rdn' (the leftmost value) or 'dn' (the whole distinguished name)
revalidate not a whole number
  ERROR directory has 'revalidate' of '-5'; it must be a whole number of seconds, zero or more
admin_groups as a bare string
  ERROR 'admin_groups' must be an array of group names; a bare string is not a list of one
admin_groups with an empty entry
  ERROR 'admin_groups' contains an entry that is not a group name
